	"nodes":[
		{
			"id":"a0a1dc62b099d291",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"macro Loop\n1. Anthurium gains ichor\n2. Ichor flows to the core\n3. ichor is spent on blooming\n4. plant hunts for more ichor\n\nmicro loop (every few seconds)\n1. heartbeat activates\n2. bloom potential flows from the core to roots, roots to roots, roots to ends.\n3. when bulb gets more bloom potential, check if threshold is passed\n\tif threshold passed, send signal to core to bloom\n\tbloom event activates, ichor is spent\n\tbloom potential value from all bulbs are cleared\n\ncreate a root\n\tinbound connections\n\toutbound connections\n\taccessories",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-520,
			"y":-160,
			"width":640,
			"height":440
		},
		{
			"id":"d29a5bda572c9c86",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n##### Flowering\nThe Anthurium has a small chance to do one of these things every heartbeat.\n\n- Extends a root 2-3 tiles in a direction toward the nearest unclaimed space\n- Spawns a single passive creature near a root end (ex this i think, this will be the responsibility of an accessory)\n- Releases an ichor mote that drifts toward the nearest hungry creature (??????????????????????)\n- Reinforces a wall tile near a root (raises hardness) (visually hardwood)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-460,
			"y":-540,
			"width":520,
			"height":340
		},
		{
			"id":"f8b55401a3ae33ad",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"```gdscript\nextends Node\nclass_name AnthuriumInterface\n\nvar esoterica: Esoterica\n\nfunc select_bloom_event(esoterica: Esoterica) -> BloomEvent:\n\tvar best_event: BloomEvent\n\tvar best_score: float = -INF\n\tfor event in bloom_events:\n\t\tvar similarity: float = esoterica.cosine_similarity(event.archetype)\n\t\tif similarity > best_score:\n\t\t\tbest_score = similarity\n\t\t\tbest_event = event\n\treturn best_event\n\t\nfunc trigger_bloom(source: Entity) -> void:\n\tvar esoterica: Esoterica = get_current_esoterica()\n\tvar event: BloomEvent = select_bloom_event(esoterica)\n\tvar potency: float = esoterica.magnitude()\n\tevent.execute(potency)\n\nfunc grow_new_accessory(source: Entity) -> Entity:\n\t# some algorithm to determine which type of plant part to spawn in\n\tvar accessory: Entity\n\treturn accessory\n\n```\n\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":-940,
			"width":720,
			"height":580
		},
		{
			"id":"7e0e5312c927f225",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"how performant are signals? wait i dont need signals\n\nroots are gonna be like a linked list that you can recursively search through.\nmake a recursive function that finds the end of each list.\nthere might be an issue with roots that have multiple connections\n\tall that really needs to be known is which direction each node \"faces\"\n\tif a connection points into the root, then bloom potential flows out of that and ichor flows in\n\tif a connection points out of the root, then bloom potential flows into that and ichor flows out",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-580,
			"y":320,
			"width":640,
			"height":340
		},
		{
			"id":"4f02e881a84316a9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n```gdscript\nextends Entity\nclass_name AnthuriumHeart\n\nvar interface: AnthuriumInterface\n\nvar next: Array[Entity]\nvar prev: Array[Entity]\n\nvar accessories: Array[Entity]\n\nvar bloom_potential: float = 0.0\n\nvar base_heartbeat_strength: float = 1.0\n\nfunc heartbeat() -> void:\n\tvar strength: float = base_heartbeat_strength + randf_range(0.1, 0.5)\n\tfor part in next:\n\t\tpart.heartbeat(strength)\n\tfor part in accessories:\n\t\tpart.heartbeat(strength)\n\n```",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":920,
			"y":-940,
			"width":580,
			"height":580
		},
		{
			"id":"3a453a4c45ae3168",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"```gdscript\nextends Entity\nclass_name AnthuriumRoot\n\nvar interface: AnthuriumInterface\n\nvar next: Array[Entity]\nvar prev: Array[Entity]\n\nvar accessories: Array[Entity]\n\nvar bloom_potential: float = 0.0\n\nvar accessory_growth_chance: float = 0.01\n\nfunc heartbeat(strength: float) -> void:\n\tbloom_potential += strength\n\tfor part in next:\n\t\tpart.push_bloom_potential(strength)\n\t\t\n\tfor part in accessories:\n\t\tpart.push_bloom_potential(strength)\n\t\t\n\tif randf() <= accessory_growth_chance:\n\t\tinterface.grow_new_accessory(self)\n\n```",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1520,
			"y":-940,
			"width":560,
			"height":580
		},
		{
			"id":"3fad1105d0bb7059",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n```gdscript\nextends Entity\nclass_name AnthuriumFlower\n\nvar interface: AnthuriumInterface\n\nvar bloom_potential: float = 0.0\nvar bloom_threshold: float = 100.0\n\n\n\nfunc heartbeat(strength: float) -> void:\n\tbloom_potential += strength\n\t\n\tif bloom_potential >= bloom_threshold:\n\t\tinterface.trigger_bloom(self)\n\t\t\n\t\t\n```",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2100,
			"y":-940,
			"width":400,
			"height":580
		},
		{
			"id":"acf2cacb5c064802",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"```gdscript\nextends Entity\nclass_name AnthuriumAccessory\n\nvar interface: AnthuriumInterface\n\nvar bloom_potential: float = 0.0\n\nfunc heartbeat(strength: float) -> void:\n\tbloom_potential += strength\n\t# some behavior or effect?\n\t# i could see this either being a one-shot thing, a timer, \n\t# or a unique behavior guided by a state machine\n\t# how do i make this composed so that this function is universal?\n```\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":2520,
			"y":-940,
			"width":580,
			"height":580
		},
		{
			"id":"62bf54ba07fb414d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\n```gdscript\nextends Variant\nclass_name Esoterica\n\nvar felicity: float\nvar furor: float\nvar lacuna: float\nvar tremendum: float\nvar acedia: float\nvar anamnesis: float\n\nfunc _init(fe: float = 0.0, fu: float = 0.0, la: float = 0.0, tr: float = 0.0, ac: float = 0.0, an: float = 0.0) -> void:\n\tfelicity = fe\n\tfuror = fu\n\tlacuna = la\n\ttremendum = tr\n\tacedia = ac\n\tanamnesis = an\n\nfunc to_array() -> Array[float]:\n\treturn [felicity, furor, lacuna, tremendum, acedia, anamnesis]\n\nfunc magnitude() -> float:\n\treturn sqrt(felicity**2 + furor**2 + lacuna**2 + tremendum**2 + acedia**2 + anamnesis**2)\n\nfunc normalized() -> Esoterica:\n\tvar m: float = magnitude()\n\tif m == 0.0: return Esoterica.new()\n\treturn Esoterica.new(felicity/m, furor/m, lacuna/m, tremendum/m, acedia/m, anamnesis/m)\n\nfunc dot(other: Esoterica) -> float:\n\treturn felicity*other.felicity + furor*other.furor + lacuna*other.lacuna + tremendum*other.tremendum + acedia*other.apophenia + anamnesis*other.anamnesis\n\nfunc cosine_similarity(other: Esoterica) -> float:\n\tvar denom: float = magnitude() * other.magnitude\n\tif denom == 0.0: return 0.0\n\treturn dot(other) / denom\n\n```",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":-220,
			"width":1140,
			"height":800
		}
